        "dropdown_more": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "settings": {
            "show": true,
            "title": "Tell me more",
            "open": false,
            "link_label": "",
            "link": "",
            "pending_text": "",
            "show_pending": false,
            "text": "<p>The staple in most meals does nothing for your protein target, so every gram has to come from the meat, and by the third day of the same dish you are done with it. ProTEGO is made to be the part of the meal that counts. It is an Asian noodle with 31.9g of protein and 12.7g of fibre per 100g, which is 25.5g and 10.2g in an 80g pack, built from four ingredients and nothing else. It cooks in five minutes, tastes like soba, and takes on whatever you cook it in, so the same pack is laksa on Monday and cold soba on Tuesday. Low GI, very low in sodium, no MSG, no preservatives, 100% plant-based.</p>"
          }
        },
        "dropdown_inside": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "settings": {
            "show": true,
            "title": "What's inside",
            "open": false,
            "link_label": "",
            "link": "",
            "pending_text": "",
            "show_pending": false,
            "text": "<p>Four ingredients: highland green barley flour, gluten, peanut protein powder and sweet potato fibre powder. No MSG, no additives, no preservatives, 100% plant-based.</p><p>Per 80g pack: 25.5g protein, 10.2g fibre, 31.8g carbohydrate, 272 kcal. One pack is one serving.<br>Per 100g: 31.9g protein, 12.7g fibre, 39.7g carbohydrate, 3.2g sugar, 2.5g fat, 9.16mg sodium.</p><p>The protein is second-life protein made from oil meals. The sweet potato fibre is a by-product of potato noodle production.</p><p>Contains gluten and peanut. Manufactured on shared equipment with soy and sesame.</p>"
          }
        },
        "dropdown_cook": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "settings": {
            "show": true,
            "title": "How to cook it",
            "open": false,
            "link_label": "",
            "link": "",
            "pending_text": "",
            "show_pending": false,
            "text": "<p>Boil one 80g pack for five minutes and drain, or cook it straight in the stock, soup or stew you are making. Add an egg, a slice of fish or whatever protein you have, then a sauce or a soup: dashi, laksa, sesame and soy, pesto.</p><p>One pack cooks up to 2.4 times its dry weight, so it fills a bowl. Use it anywhere you would use soba, ramen, udon or spaghetti. It holds its shape through long cooking, and the next day in a meal prep box.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
